# Activity scene — saying yes to the coworker, first time. cast.md § 5.1: the
# coworker never moralizes when the player declines things; doesn't try to
# save the player. dialogue-context.md § 3: "worldly" / "bad association".
# TODO: authenticity check

A bar on Fifth, the music a little too loud. You order a soda with lime so it looks like something.
{GameState.coworker_name} introduces you to everyone as "the only person at work who actually reads the memos." Someone asks what you did last weekend.
- "Volunteer work."
	"They do this door-to-door thing," {GameState.coworker_name} says. "It's actually kind of brave. I couldn't do it."
- "I was preaching, actually. Door to door."
	[signal arg="CONVICTION:1"]
	A small silence, and then someone says "Huh, respect," and means it, and the conversation moves on to someone's terrible landlord.
Nobody asks you anything you'd have to answer. You're home by ten. The phone buzzes: "glad u came 🙂"
